  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustainable Rural Life: Socio-Participatory Technical Assistance</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cooperativa de Agricultores Ecolgicos do Portal da Amaznia (Cooperagrepa) will use a community-based extension service to develop the network of farmers applying &quot;agroecological&quot; methods that protect biodiversity and maximize production of an area extending over 19,730 square miles in northern Mato Grosso. Work also includes the development of a system for certifying production as organic so that farmers benefit from the premium paid by ethical consumers. This project will benefit 350 Brazilians directly and another 1,200 indirectly.</narrative>
  </description>
